- Runtime Environment: Node.js v24 on Ubuntu 18.04 (GLIBC 2.28 in ~/glibc-2.28/build).
- Native Engine Ban: STRICTLY NO Prisma, NO Tailwind v4 Oxide, NO native C/Rust binaries.
- Stack: Next.js 15 App Router, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS v3.4 (PostCSS), Drizzle ORM with postgres.js, shadcn/ui.
- Code Structure:
  - All mortgage calculations (P&I, Amortization, APR, DTI) must be pure functions isolated in `/lib/mortgage-math/`.
  - All schemas and database models live in `/db/schema.ts`.
  - Server Actions handle all database mutations in `/actions/`.
- Styling: navy-and-gold branding from the VanDyke logo (`public/brand/`), on an exchange-style
  rate board. Tokens live in `tailwind.config.ts`:
  - `ink` = logo navy chrome (#050D18 / #0B192C / #3A4A63 / #8A97AA / #E7EBF1), `canvas` #F7F5F1.
  - `brand` = logo gold #C9A44C. Use `brand-300` for text on navy, `brand-500` for fills,
    `brand-600`+ for text on light. Never white text on gold — it fails contrast; use `text-ink-950`.
  - `up` #0E9F6E / `down` #E5484D for market direction only. A falling mortgage rate prints green.
- Typography: `font-sans` DM Sans for prose, `font-display` Inter Tight (bold, tight tracking) for headings,
  `font-brand` Playfair Display for the logo wordmark only, `font-mono` IBM Plex Mono for all figures.
  Use the `.tape` utility for any rate, price, or payment number.
- Surfaces: navy chrome (ticker, navbar, hero, rate board, footer) on `ink-950`; light data sections on
  `canvas`/white with `rounded-board` corners and hairline `ink/10` borders.
- Imagery: warm lifestyle photography in `public/images/`, Unsplash-licensed and credited in
  `public/images/CREDITS.md`. Never copy imagery from other lenders' sites — theirs is Adobe Stock
  or Getty licensed and does not transfer. Import photos statically so the demo `basePath` holds.
